user_message:
Review every unordered pair using local zero-based indices, not hypothesis IDs.
Preserve all feature fields and report exact pending alignment differences.

[
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 16,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_comment_personal_labor_process_detail",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments"
      ],
      "definition": "Any counter-argument comment in OC_comments: introduces concrete, personal (first-hand or specific-person) details of how work/labor is actually done (tasks, workflow, conditions, procedures)",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read the JSON list in OC_comments (comments by users other than OP; order carries no meaning). Return 1 if at least one comment itself introduces concrete labor-process details drawn from personal experience (the commenter's or a specific named/described person's job), e.g. specific tasks, workflow steps, shifts, tools, conditions, or procedures of actual work. Generic abstract statements about work, hypothetical examples without specific process detail, and quoted OP text do not count. Return 0 if the list is parsed and no comment does so. Return null if OC_comments is missing, empty, or unparseable."
    }
  },
  {
    "hypothesis_id": 27,
    "feature": {
      "name": "any_comment_personal_anecdote",
      "dtype": "binary",
      "source_columns": [
        "OC_comments"
      ],
      "definition": "Any counter-argument comment in OC_comments: relates a concrete personal anecdote (commenter's own specific lived experience or event) as part of its argument.",
      "kind": "prompt",
      "spec": "Read the OC_comments JSON list (comments by users other than the OP; order carries no meaning). Return 1 if at least one comment's own text recounts a concrete personal anecdote: a specific experience, event or situation that the commenter (or someone they personally know, stated as first-hand) lived through, e.g. 'when I worked at X, ...'. Generic hypotheticals, statistics, general facts, others' reported studies, quotations of the OP, and hypothetical 'imagine' scenarios do not count. Return 0 if all comments are assessable and none has such an anecdote. Return null if OC_comments is missing, unparseable or an empty list. Do not use any other column."
    }
  }
]

Submit {"comparisons": [...]} covering every pair with a verdict and reason.
